WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.969
-Kate Upton, thank you
for being here.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.971
Thank you for playing along
with Ken as well,

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:05.904
earlier in our game.

00:00:05.904 --> 00:00:06.906
You've met Ken before.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.108
You worked with him before.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:11.444
-Yes. Yeah, I was
on his first photo shoot.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.379
So obviously I taught him
everything I know.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:14.547
-Yeah.
-About modeling.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.348
-Of course, yeah.
-I was a great mentor.

00:00:16.348 --> 00:00:18.584
-What was it like working with
Ken on a photo shoot?

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.953
-Oh, it was so great.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:23.856
I mean, he is so funny
in the shots,

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:28.194
but then behind the scenes he's
like, "Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.362
I'm a physician.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.030
I shouldn't be holding it
like a pool noodle."

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.966
But I was like,
"You just got to lean in,"

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.334
and that's why he looks so sexy.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.368
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.636
Holding up,
with that pool noodle.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.904
-It doesn't make any sense until
you see this photo.

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:40.239
Here's a photo of Ken and Kate.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.608
See if you can tell
the difference, who's who.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:43.776
-It's hard to tell.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:47.547
-Ken is --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.015
What is he doing?

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.551
He's lost his -- He's absolutely
lost his -- He's lost his mind.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.253
[ Laughter ]
He's lost his mind.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.187
-And they kept being like,
"Don't --"

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:56.322
-"Don't look at me."

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.324
-"Don't look at him.
Don't look at him."

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.426
And he was, like,
fully into that noodle.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:01.660
-How have you been?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.730
I'm sorry to make you remember
those memories.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.697
How have you been?

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.032
Talk to me about Strong4Me.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.600
You guys are growing, expanding.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.902
-Yes. I'm so excited because,
you know,

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:12.004
we're all about
inside-out health.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.641
So we're expanding into
a full wellness brand,

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.343
and next we're going to tackle
mental wellness,

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.045
which I think is so important.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.847
It's not just about working out.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:23.249
It's also about staying
mentally healthy.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:27.253
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's great.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.688
It's taken a while, but it's
actually happened pretty fast

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:32.325
if you think about it because
when we talked about this

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:35.094
years ago when you thought about
this idea and started it,

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.095
but good.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.596
-I know.
The community keeps growing,

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:40.065
and it's just so awesome to hear
everyone's stories

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:42.101
and keep the positive
inspiration going.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.036
-You said
that your daughter Genevieve

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:45.271
is an inspiration to you.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.606
-Yes. She's the cutest.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.174
-Look at this little nugget.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.675
-Well, she's 14 months now.

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:52.145
I learned that moms
have to say the months.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.480
-You say the months? Yeah.
-That's what moms do.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.781
-She's so cute.

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:59.652
If she wanted to go into
modeling, would you allow her?

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.087
Would you say yes?

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:04.624
-I mean, we're all about passion
in our family.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:07.226
So if she feels really
passionate about anything,

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.761
you know, I know Justin and I

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.564
will fully support her with
whatever she wants to do.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.633
And if it's modeling,
I have a few tips.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:15.968
I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.537
-Yeah. Yeah, you had a pretty --
-I did mentor Ken so...

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:19.973
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:23.209
She doesn't want to end up
in that direction at all. Yeah.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.945
I saw somewhere that you were
learning jiu-jitsu.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.313
Are you still into that?

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.648
-Oh, my God.
I'm obsessed with jiu-jitsu.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.884
I just earned my first stripe
and I --

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.086
-Now, how does that work,
the stripes?

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:37.924
-So, you get your belt,
and then you earn three stripes,

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.459
and you go to the next color.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:42.227
So I just got my first one,
and the test is so hard,

00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:44.697
and you learn all these
different submissions,

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.633
how to break someone's arm,
how to pop the shoulder out,

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.902
how to choke them out,
and they test you.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.137
How many chokes do you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:54.306
You know, and I --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:55.708
I was so into it.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.743
I would practice everywhere,
and my test was right after

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:58.878
the World Series and --

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.146
-And you passed?
-Yeah.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.248
Well, I was practicing,
you know, on Justin,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.116
on his whole family,
my mother-in-law.

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.585
-He's in the World Series.
What are you talking about?

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:08.754
-Well, he would only let me
practice on him --

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.422
-Your mother-in-law.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:12.825
What's wrong with you?
Why are you taking jiu-jitsu?

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.261
-You know, 'cause I want to
beat someone up.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.363
[ Laughter ]
-No, you don't. Come on.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.065
-I just want to know how.
I just want to know how.

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.400
I just want to know how.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.536
-Are you flipping people
around and --

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:24.737
-Yeah.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.438
-Jiu-jitsu's like MMA type of
stuff, right?

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:27.907
-Yeah. Yep, yep.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.575
-There's part boxing, jiu-jitsu.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:30.843
-Everything.
-Yep.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.245
-So right now you're flipping
people around.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:34.914
-Yes.
-You go to a place --

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.015
-Actually, I was --
I accidentally --

00:03:37.015 --> 00:03:38.250
I was showing Justin,

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.720
and I accidentally flipped him
in our kitchen.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.555
-What?
-And his foot hit, like,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:47.694
the corner of our island, and he
really just hammed that up.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:51.197
It was like a cut this big,
and he was like, "I'm injured!

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:53.666
"I'm injured!"
I was like, "Calm down.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:58.938
It's not your right arm."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.307
-Could you teach me a move
and all of us a move in case?

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.075
-Yes, yes.
Of course, of course. Okay.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:04.410
-Alright, let's do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.647
-So, technically
I only have one stripe.

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:08.914
I'm not, like, safety certified.

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:10.216
-Okay.
-But it's fine.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.051
Just make sure to tap
if you feel, like, panicked.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.853
-Tap if I feel panicked?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.654
[ Laughter ]
'Cause I don't know my limits.

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.189
Okay, so,
if you're coming at me --

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.591
-Okay, so wait. First of all,
why are you already like this?

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:21.460
-Because I'm in my fight stance.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.661
-But if you're doing this,

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:24.330
that means that you want me
to come at you?

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.566
If you're like, "Hey, Jimmy,"
what do you want me to do?

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.733
I go, "What's your problem?"

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:29.201
Of course,
I'm going to run to you

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:30.803
and jump in your arms
if you do that.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.871
So, alright, so you do that
and I -- What do I do?

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:34.373
Like, do you want me
to attack you?

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.175
-Yeah, just if you were
walking like, yeah.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.377
Come like you're attacking me.
-What are you gonna do?

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.246
Can you just tell me
what you're going to do?

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:41.947
[ Laughter ]
Just tell me what you're gonna

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.382
do because I don't
want have to --

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.585
What if my instincts fight back?
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:46.819
-It's okay. I can take you down.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.920
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.322
And by the way,
you probably can.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.424
Alright. Alright.
So, I'm walking?

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.926
-Okay, I'm going to do
the rear naked choke hold.

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:54.726
-Say it again.

00:04:54.726 --> 00:04:55.895
-The rear naked choke.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.963
-We're doing
the rear naked choke hold?

00:04:57.963 --> 00:04:59.232
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:01.600
-Let's do it, man.
I mean, let's go for it, man.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.737
At this point.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:08.073
Honey, turn the channel.

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:10.309
-Okay, so walk towards me.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:13.245
-Okay, just walk towards you.
-Yep, and then I would just --

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:15.915
-Oh, man. Oh, man.
Alright, that's good.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.049
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.751
-No, you got to tap out
with your hand.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.653
-Oh, I thought
you meant tapping --

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:23.422
I already tapped out. I was
tapping out. I was tapping.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.357
[ Cheers and applause ]
That was a good hold.

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.093
How do you do that?
You press really --

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.394
-Yeah, yeah.
-You pass out?

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.029
I'm really passing out
a little bit.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.464
What were you doing?

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.333
-Yeah, it takes -- it takes
12 seconds to fully pass out.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.101
-Wait, how many seconds
did you do that?

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.502
[ Laughter ]
-I wasn't even --

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.037
As soon as you tapped,
I stopped.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.872
Even the tap dancing.
-That was like a --

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.873
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.007
That was a five-second
tap dance.

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:43.542
You did it like seven --
Alright.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.678
Here, it's happening again.
Kate Upton, everyone.

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:48.547
Check out Strong4Me Fitness.

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:50.549
Old Dominion
performs for us next.

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:52.919
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back. Wow.

